body:
This is a maybe red flag, just having a quick look at the code for what may be causing this (I don't currently have hardware setup to quickly test), [render_scene_buffers_gles3.cpp lines 383 - 402, method _check_render_buffers](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/drivers/gles3/storage/render_scene_buffers_gles3.cpp#L383):
```
		} else if (use_internal_buffer) {
			// We can combine MSAA and scaling/effects.
			msaa3d.needs_resolve = false;
			msaa3d.check_fbo_cache = false;

			// We render to our internal textures, MSAA is only done in tile memory only.
			// On mobile this means MSAA never leaves tile memory = efficiency!
			glGenFramebuffers(1, &msaa3d.fbo);
			glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, msaa3d.fbo);

			_rt_attach_textures(internal3d.color, internal3d.depth, msaa3d.samples, view_count, true);

			GLenum status = glCheckFramebufferStatus(GL_FRAMEBUFFER);
			if (status != GL_FRAMEBUFFER_COMPLETE) {
				_clear_msaa3d_buffers();
				msaa3d.mode = RSE::VIEWPORT_MSAA_DISABLED;
				WARN_PRINT("Could not create 3D MSAA framebuffer, status: " + texture_storage->get_framebuffer_error(status));
			}

			glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, GLES3::TextureStorage::system_fbo);
```

In the situation that `rt_msaa_supported`/`rt_msaa_multiview_supported` is true, as we already discussed, we don't allocate an msaa buffer, hence `msaa.color` stays zero.
This means that in the scenario that we have an intermediate buffer, and MSAA is enabled, this code is run every time `_check_render_buffers` is called and we create another FBO. That is likely the leak.

We should likely check `msaa3d.fbo` instead of `msaa3d.color` to check if we've already allocated things.

So [line 205 - 208](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/drivers/gles3/storage/render_scene_buffers_gles3.cpp#L205) becomes:
```
	if ((!use_internal_buffer || internal3d.color != 0) && (msaa3d.mode == RSE::VIEWPORT_MSAA_DISABLED || msaa3d.fbo != 0)) {
		// already setup!
		return;
	}
```

And I think [line 280](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/drivers/gles3/storage/render_scene_buffers_gles3.cpp#L280) should become something like:
```
	if (msaa3d.mode != RSE::VIEWPORT_MSAA_DISABLED) {
		if (msaa3d.fbo != 0) {
			// already setup!
			return;
		}
```
(note bringing the fbo check inside of the if block, or else we end up overwriting our msaa samples settings)

If `rt_msaa_supported`/`rt_msaa_multiview_supported` is true, and we're not scaling, we don't get an fbo here as we check our fbo cache. But the code that gets run repeatedly is harmless in this scenario.

If someone could test [this PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124643) before I have a chance to do it myself, that be swell.
